Draw the border of a faded menu item

The paint of a selected menu item tests the fade appearance before the
border option. The fade branch paints the gradient alone and no border.
The box for the border of a menu item therefore has no effect under the
fade appearance. Fade is the shipped value, and the tooltip of the box
promises a border around the gradient.

The fade branch now draws the border while the box holds true. The
border takes the standard border shade of the menu colours, which is the
shade that the other appearances draw through the light bevel. A menu
item with the box false keeps the paint of before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 21 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

